:: Avery Valentines 11
/* ============ 번역 필요 ============== */
<<effects>>

<<switch $avery_valentines.talk>>
<<case "sparkling_water">>
	<<set $averySeen.pushUnique("sparkling_water")>>
	<<if $speech_attitude is "meek" or $speech_attitude_avery>>
		"If you don't mind me asking," you say. "What happened? At the end of that story about how you almost died of thirst, I mean."
	<<elseif $speech_attitude is "bratty">>
		"I can't believe you cut off that story right when it was getting good," you say. "Come on, what happened? How'd you almost die of thirst?"
	<<else>>
		"What happened back then?" you ask. "How did you almost die of thirst?"
	<</if>>
	<br><br>
	<<if C.npc.Avery.love gte 50>>
		Avery <<laughs>>. "Well, I only drank sparkling water, and there was none to be found." <<He>> shrugs one shoulder as if that answers that. "But I survived. That adventure, as well as a number of others." There's a mysterious smile on <<his>> face.
	<<elseif $avery_valentines.soften>>
		Avery huffs a laugh. "Suffice it to say it was for a silly reason. I'm certain you've had some of those moments of your own."
	<<else>>
		"Never mind that." Avery waves a hand as if discouraging a fly. "<<person2>><<He>> was exaggerating, as one typically does when telling stories about one's youth."
	<</if>>
	<br><br>
	<<person1>>
<<case "university_friend">>
	<<set $averySeen.pushUnique("university_friend")>>
	You ask about that friend of Avery's.
	<br><br>
	Avery <<= $averyragerevealed is 1 ? "rolls <<his>> eyes" : "sighs">>. "Don't mind <<person2>><<him>>. <<He>> used to revel in inappropriate behaviour." <<person1>><<His>> lip curls. "And it appears <<person2>><<he>> hasn't changed a bit. No wonder <<he>> was surprised to see that I had."
	<br><br>
	<<person1>>
<<case "mansion2">>
	<<if $phase is 1>> /* Like it */
		You tell Avery that you like living with <<him>>. It's an upgrade from life at the orphanage.
		<br><br>
		Avery listens to your answer with a growing smile. "Is that so? Why, I'm glad to hear it."
		<br><br>
		<<if C.npc.Avery.love gte 60>>
			"I enjoy having you around, too. I see that
		<<elseif $avery_mansion?.days_absent gte 7>>
			"Though it's hard to believe when I haven't seen you around in over a week. Still, at least
		<<else>>
			"I see that
		<</if>>
		living with Bailey has given you an appreciation for the finer things in life," <<he>> muses. "Speaking of Bailey, what was it like living with your old caretaker?"
		<br><br>
	<<elseif $phase is 2>> /* Noncommittal */
		You muddle through a response, avoiding taking one stance or another. It wouldn't do to offend Avery.
		<br><br>
		Avery listens to your answer with a smile and a raised brow. "An interesting answer. I suppose living with Bailey in the orphanage has left you at a loss in the face of luxury." <<He>> laughs to <<himself>>. "Speaking of Bailey, what was it like living with your old caretaker?"
		<br><br>
	<<else>> /* Dislike it */
		You tell Avery you don't like living in <<his>> mansion. You didn't expect to have to <<= $avery_mansion?.jobs.includes("lounge") ? "cook and clean" : "cook dinner">> when you were taken in.
		<br><br>
		Avery raises an eyebrow as you speak. When you're finished, <<he>> <<laughs>>, unfazed by your criticism<<if $averyragerevealed is 1>> to your surprise<</if>>.
		<br><br>
		"My, my. Is it so bad to have work to do?" <<he>> asks. "It builds character, after all. Besides, my paying Bailey for you means you're earning far more than any team of professional cleaners would. All it takes is a little bit of work and time out of your day, and you needn't worry a bit about <<nnpc_him "Bailey">>."
		<br><br>
		<<He>> leans back in <<his>> seat, and asks, "Speaking of Bailey, what was it like living with your old caretaker?"
		<br><br>
	<</if>>

	<<link [[Say it was terrible|Avery Valentines 11]]>><<set $avery_valentines.talk to "bailey">><<set $phase to 1>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Answer noncommittally|Avery Valentines 11]]>><<set $avery_valentines.talk to "bailey">><<set $phase to 2>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Say you're grateful towards Bailey|Avery Valentines 11]]>><<set $avery_valentines.talk to "bailey">><<set $phase to 3>><</link>>
	<br>
<<case "bailey">>
	<<if $phase is 1>> /* Terrible */
		<<if $speech_attitude is "meek" or $speech_attitude_avery>>
			"It was miserable, to be honest," you say, your face crumpling.
		<<elseif $speech_attitude is "bratty">>
			"Oh, it sucked," you say with a scowl.
		<<else>>
			"It was terrible," you say with a frown.
		<</if>> You tell Avery a few stories of Bailey's cruelty towards the orphans.
		<br><br>
		Avery listens and nods here and there. When you're finished, <<he>> says, "<<nnpc_He "Bailey">> seems to be quite the tyrant. It's a good thing I saved you from <<nnpc_him "Bailey">>, isn't it?<<if C.npc.Avery.dom gte 60>> You ought to thank me more often.<</if>>"
		<br><br>
		<<He>> then waves a dismissive hand as if to ward off a fly. "But enough about <<nnpc_him "Bailey">>.<<if $avery_valentines.soften>> Tonight is about us.<</if>>"
		<br><br>
	<<elseif $phase is 2>> /* Noncommittal */
		<<if $speech_attitude is "meek" or $speech_attitude_avery>>
			"It was fine," you say.
		<<elseif $speech_attitude is "bratty">>
			"It was whatever," you say with a shrug.
		<<else>>
			"It had its ups and downs," you say with a shrug.
		<</if>>
		<br><br>
		You don't offer anything else of substance. Avery seems a bit disappointed, and soon waves a dismissive hand as if to ward off a fly. "Well, enough about <<nnpc_him "Bailey">>.<<if $avery_valentines.soften>> Tonight is about us.<</if>>"
		<br><br>
	<<else>> /* Grateful */
		<<if $speech_attitude is "meek" or $speech_attitude_avery>>
			"I'm actually very grateful for <<nnpc_him "Bailey">>," you say.
		<<elseif $speech_attitude is "bratty">>
			"It was fine. <<nnpc_He "Bailey">>'d help us out here and there," you say with a shrug.
		<<else>>
			"It was all right," you say. "I'm actually pretty grateful for Bailey. <<nnpc_Hes "Bailey">> helped us out a lot."
		<</if>> You tell Avery a few stories of how Bailey has helped the orphans.
		<br><br>
		Avery listens, but appears to be unmoved by them, giving the odd acknowledging hum here and there. When you're finished, <<he>> gives a <<= $averyragerevealed is 1 ? "feigned" : "wry">> smile, and says, "I think you've mistaken Bailey's motives, <<pcpetname "Avery">>. <<nnpc_He "Bailey">> is far from a saint."
		<br><br>
		<<He>> then waves a dismissive hand as if to ward off a fly. "But enough about <<nnpc_him "Bailey">>.<<if $avery_valentines.soften>> Tonight is about us.<</if>>"
		<br><br>
	<</if>>
<<case "remy_past">>
	<<set $averySeen.pushUnique("remy_past")>>
	You ask how long Avery has known Remy.
	<br><br>
	"I've known Remy since university, though we were both aware of each other before then," Avery answers. "Similar circles, you see. <<nnpc_He "Remy">> and I, as well as a small coterie, including the <<person2>><<gentleman_npc>> you just met, would often meet together for various activities."
	<br><br>
	"Even back then, I knew Remy was destined for success. But <<nnpc_he "Remy">> was always too..." <<person1>><<He>> drums <<his>> fingers on the table for a few moments as <<he>> thinks. "Rigid is the word for it, I suppose. <<nnpc_He "Remy">> missed out on more than one golden opportunity back then. I would let <<nnpc_him "Remy">> know it, too."
	<br><br>
	"And now?"
	<br><br>
	"Now," Avery
	<<if $avery_fate is "ascended">>
		frowns and shakes <<his>> head. "Now I don't bother. Neither of us are who we were back then. Though Remy is as stubborn as ever."
	<<elseif $avery_fate is "saved">>
		frowns a little, and <<his>> gaze goes somewhat distant. "Now I wonder if things could have gone differently." <<He>> continues, but trails off, then sighs. "In any case, Remy is much the same. Though things have rather changed of late."
	<<else>>
		shrugs. "Now I keep such things to myself. It's not as if <<nnpc_he "Remy">> would listen, anyway," <<he>> murmurs.
	<</if>>
	<br><br>
<<case "trading_card">>
	<<set $averySeen.pushUnique("trading_card")>>
	"About that trading card I gave you," you start.
	<br><br>
	"Ah, that." Avery cocks <<his>> head a little and scrutinises you. "Just where did you get it, exactly? It wasn't just some common card you'd given me."
	<br><br>
	You say you got it from a friend.
	<br><br>
	"I see." <<His>> eyes drift shut as <<he>> takes a sip from <<his>> wine. "Well, it's just
	<<if $avery_fate is "saved">>
		from a silly game." <<He>> pauses, and a nostalgic look crosses <<his>> face. "I used to play it with my friends, once upon a time. Of course, that was back when I was a child. I don't know why you decided to give it to me of all people."
	<<elseif $avery_fate is "ascended">>
		a card from some silly game meant for children," <<he>> says. "To be frank, I don't know why you gave it to me. It's of no use."
	<<else>>
		from some silly game," <<he>> says with a shrug. "I don't know why you decided to give it to me of all people."
	<</if>>
	<br><br>
	<<if $speech_attitude is "meek" or $speech_attitude_avery>>
		"Oh." You give <<him>> a confused look. "Isn't it why you forgave me, though?"
	<<elseif $speech_attitude is "bratty">>
		"Wait, but if you didn't want it, then why'd you forgive me when I gave it to you?"
	<<else>>
		"But isn't it why you forgave me?"
	<</if>>
	<br><br>
	Avery raises an eyebrow. "I forgave you because I could tell how desperate you were for another chance." <<He>> smirks. "That's all."
	<br><br>
<<case "trading_card2">>
	<<set $averySeen.pushUnique("trading_card2")>>
	<<if $speech_attitude is "meek" or $speech_attitude_avery>>
